sions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260908-2tkufa\n- **Title:** TASK-260908-2tkufa: bind-approved-contract-catalog-and-implementation-owners\n- **Parent:** STORY-260908-18woqo\n\n### Description\n\nRegenerate and reconcile contract catalog, traceability ownership and source-version validation after the approved normative pin is adopted. Every added or refined selector/auth/migration obligation must map to its real implementation owner; unsupported new runtime behavior must not be reported as implemented. Preserve acceptance evidence for unchanged legacy contracts and resume the existing dependent leaves after this Story lands.\n\n### Scope\n\ninternal/catalog, internal/traceability, directly required generator checks and board scope bindings; no edits to another Story partial implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nFull contract census and source references match the adopted normative source; existing and added contract obligations have non-duplicated real owners; generator/traceability gates pass and detect omissions; legacy support claims remain truthful; exact reviewed signed Story delivered before unblocking dependent code.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-implementation.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260908-2tkufa/TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-implementation.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2872`\n- Content digest: `sha256:18056889cac34939b74b635089b64684a9af12024a5e538a6982a05fc7d84126`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-recovery.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260908-2tkufa/TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-recovery.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3035`\n- Content digest: `sha256:2a076db1018da0d2e340ae11120aab8b22ea4289705a6c63ab3ccca1de4791a0`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-review-rev2.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260908-2tkufa/TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-review-rev2.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4477`\n- Content digest: `sha256:230830b7a2e228ba6222a302a6e98b0e9766866e117a04e2687ec9159a6880e3`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa_review-control-boundary.md\n# Current control-root boundary at review launch\n\nPrimary reviewer spawn initially refused worktree_control_root_dirty for the one temporary task-board.config.json gate alignment. After CR2 finished all26gates successfully, primary restored ONLY that control-root file from the producer's byte backup, first proving: currentcontrol==candidate; backup==gitHEAD; semanticdiffexactlyoneV050->V060cataloggencommand and nootherfields. Restoration outcome attached. The candidate and captured CR2 are unchanged and retainV060config. Controlroot is now deliberately its cleanV050trunkconfig until Storyland; this supersedes the earlier review brief's expectation of CURRENT root/candidate equality. Compare the candidate to captured CR2 and review itsV060command as intended. Do not overwrite the candidate with trunk or weaken stale-input refusal. Run exactcandidategates from its configuration; any lifecycleconfigdigestissue must be evidenced rather than bypassed. No new CR or source mutation is authorized for the reviewer.\n\nThis restores the temporary operational alignment, not the substantive candidate change. Producerconfig-consistency evidence describes handoff time and remains true at that time. Final Storylanding must carry the reviewedV060config into trunk.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-integration.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260908-2tkufa/TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-integration.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2969`\n- Content digest: `sha256:04a3c5f6c38ddabd9cfd939ef90d1c31c678af0f34d84b94b3778f7d1b903121`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260908-2tkufa_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260908-2tkufa, name=TASK-260908-2tkufa_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `integrating` is the role handoff status; use it only after the evidence contract is satisfied.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260908-2tkufa --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260908-18woqo.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260908-18woqo/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260908-18woqo`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED 