 integrate accepted CR2. |\\n\\nTests are candidate source awaiting the managed signed integration, deliberately not hand-committed. The accepted predecessor's cryptographic upstream tag/commit and fixture provenance review is reused; this reviewer independently checked local source census, consumers, identity and behavior, without repeating network provenance or claiming hosted CI.\\n\\n## Independent execution\\n\\nDarwin arm64, Go 1.25.5. All 26 exact candidate-configured local commands independently returned exit 0, including uncached full tests, race, coverage, vet, build, gofmt, 13 fuzz smoke commands, strict V060 catalog check, tracecheck, Linux/Windows cross-build, JSON validation and diff checks. Per-command strings, exits and outputs are attached in TASK-260908-2tkufa_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (gate-01 through gate-26). Cross-builds prove compilation, not target runtime behavior.\\n\\nTracecheck reports 63 contracts, 101 acceptance cases, 32 fixtures, 56 bindings and 17/463 discharged clauses. This does not claim runtime coverage for new contracts.\\n\\nAll 11 producer-shaped narrowing attacks were inspected and independently rerun on this exact candidate: each instrument-only behavioral suite returned 0 and emitted its marker; each mutated suite returned 1 with the expected named semantic failure. No compile/setup failure is counted. M1 legacy Generate fallback; M2 stale CI root; M3 legacy traceability fallback; M4 stale Current; M5 omitted selector owner; M6 stale directive with token preserved; M7 Config-4 Decode admission; M8 stale configured command with token preserved; M9 only section 14.7.1 admission; M10 only reader4 admission; M11 only migration target4 admission. M6's static token control passes while its behavioral suite fails. Full pristine/restored controls pass, and scratch restoration is byte-exact. The archive contains applicators, applied diffs where emitted, named failures and actual exits; M11 has separate records. This is targeted adoption evidence, not an exhaustive historical mutation score.\\n\\n## Non-blocking evidence qualifications\\n\\n- Candidate V060 config matches captured CR2. Clean control root intentionally retains trunk V050 per the explicit launch boundary; no equality with control root is asserted now. Signed integration must carry the candidate V060 invocation.\\n- The configured bare `task-board validate` exits 0 but prints 2,225 activity/ledger issues and appears to resolve the checkout board. An additional explicit authoritative-board validation also exits 0 but prints 231 activity/ledger issues. Neither is described as a clean board-health result. Producer CR2 already shows the same configured 2,225-issue result. This review does not alter validation policy or repair unrelated board history; live owner queries and exact repository tests supply the task-specific evidence.\\n- Five appended historical scope strings encode section signs as literal backslash-u00a7. Independent comparison confirms unchanged section numbers and remaining text, and all six prior AC strings are exactly retained. This is a presentation anomaly, not loss of ownership or an omitted obligation. A future authorized board-text cleanup should normalize those signs; reviewer made no scope mutation.\\n- Older descriptive gap prose such as the Section17.1 “every pinned” reader phrase should be read under the explicit adoption bounds and Config-4 refusal tests; it is not runtime support evidence. The new adoption document and executable tests explicitly refuse Config4 support.\\n- Reviewer probes initially used a nonexistent local skill path, an unsupported resource-read spelling, a guessed historical document filename, and a regular-file hash for the CLAUDE symlink. Correct paths/resource-get/link hashing were used for final evidence. Scope byte comparison exposed the encoding anomaly above; it was not silently counted as byte preservation.\\n\\nAccept revision 2 through accept_cr and route to integrating. Do not checkpoint this final leaf manually, supply commit_ack, mutate the Story branch, activate dependents, or mark done in review. The orchestrator should route the exact producer role/archetype for signed Story integration and publication review/check lifecycle. Any integration config-digest refusal must be evidenced and resolved through the lifecycle, never bypassed.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9081,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2271,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
