{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb1d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0873d-82d6-7f93-a2e2-bf53a69e7049"},"sequence":1001,"recorded_at":1780531400001997,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65a48f0a-55bb-4f9b-8e39-974e25aa8246","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"65a48f0a-55bb-4f9b-8e39-974e25aa8246","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65a48f0a-55bb-4f9b-8e39-974e25aa8246"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Integration could not land: `task-board worktree integrate` refuses via two jointly unsatisfiable pre-transaction guards, so nothing was committed and trunk is unmoved.\n\nWhat happened:\n\n- Attempt 1: refused — `version_control.confirm` requires explicit `--commit-time`. Supplied it on retry.\n- Attempt 2: refused — `validation_suite_changed` (configured suite `c942b6e6…` from control-root V050 config vs evidence suite `6b6c6246…` from the candidate V060 config).\n- Proved by JSON walk that control vs candidate config differ in exactly one field: validation command 21, V050 → V060 cataloggen invocation. Temporarily aligned only that string in the control working tree (byte-equal to candidate).\n- Attempt 3: suite check passed, but refused — `1 dirty path(s) … overlap the Change Request's changed paths: task-board.config.json`.\n- `transaction show` confirms no transaction was ever recorded, so no `resolve`/`rollback` path exists. Each attempt differed by one principled variable; no unchanged retry, no bypass.\n\nState left clean: control config reverted to `ac85fa77…` (matches the reviewer's restoration record, `git status` clean); candidate worktree untouched at branch tip `b4c4349`; trunk at `2a8db96`; task stays `integrating`.\n\nEvidence attached: `TASK-260908-2tkufa_integration-outcome.md` (outcome) with verbatim refusals, suite/config digests, the deadlock analysis, and reproduction inputs. Per the brief this is a tool-contract defect for the primary's sourcefix lane — the suite check should admit evidence produced under the candidate's own suite when the CR changes that suite — so I made no source mutation and no new CR. The accepted CR2 remains valid and review-accepted, awaiting a supported lifecycle fix.","reason":null}}
